.TH CHANGELOG-REFORMAT 8 "July 2026" "changelog 1.0.0" "System Administration Commands"
.SH NAME
changelog reformat \- reformat and normalize changelog configuration files
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B changelog reformat
[\fIoptions\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.PP
The \fBreformat\fR command reformats and normalizes changelog.yaml or .changes.yaml configuration files. It ensures consistent formatting, applies default values where missing, and validates the structure of configuration data.

This is particularly useful after manual edits to config files, when merging configurations from different sources, or when preparing files for version control with consistent styling.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Show help message and exit.

.TP
\fB\-\-is\-collection\fR=\fIBOOL\fR
Override whether this is a collection project (true/false/yes/no). Affects how configuration is interpreted and reformatted.

.TP
\fB\-d\fR, \fB\-\-dir\fR=\fIPATH\fR
Changelog base directory containing config files. Defaults to current directory's \fIchangelogs/\fR subdirectory.
.SH CONFIGURATION FILES HANDLED
.PP
The reformat command processes these file types:
.RS 4
.IP \(bu 2
\fIchangelogs/config.yaml\fR \- Main project configuration with fragment settings, section definitions, and output options
.IP \(bu 2
\fI.changes.yaml\fR \- Machine-readable metadata storing version history and fragment references
.RE

.TP
.B Reformatting Actions:
.RS 4
.IP \(bu 2
Normalize YAML indentation to consistent 2-space style
.IP \(bu 2
Sort keys alphabetically within sections for readability
.IP \(bu 2
Apply default values for missing optional fields
.IP \(bu 2
Validate structure against expected schema
.IP \(bu 2
Preserve comments and formatting where possible
.RE
.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
Reformat changelog.yaml in current directory:
.nf
    changelog reformat
.fi

.TP
Reformat with custom collection namespace override:
.nf
    changelog reformat --is-collection true -d /path/to/collection
.fi

.TP
Normalize .changes.yaml metadata file:
.nf
    changelog reformat -d changelogs/
.fi
.SH SEE ALSO
.TP
\fBchangelog-config(5)\fR \- Configuration file reference and options
.TP
\fBchangelog-lint-changelog-yaml(8)\fR \- Validate configuration syntax
